     Tally colours for Emergency information (com.android.emergency). Its
     screens are light in both themes (light AppCompat and DeviceDefault
     Settings themes, no dark variant), so these read light-scheme roles and
     palette tones and have no night values.

     The reds stay red: the error role and error tones. The emergency
     information header is red under white text; the tab indicator on it,
     Material yellow before, is the error role's own on-colour, like the text.
     The teal tab indicator of the editing screens takes the accent. The
     Emergency SOS countdown screen (black, white and greys) is left as it is.
-->
<resources>
    <!-- Header of the emergency information screen, shown from the lock
         screen, and the countdown notification's colour -->
    <color name="emergency_primary">@android:color/system_error_light</color>
    <!-- Its status bar: error T30 -->
    <color name="emergency_primary_dark">@android:color/system_error_700</color>
    <!-- Text and tabs on the red header -->
    <color name="emergency_owner_text_color">@android:color/system_on_error_light</color>
    <color name="tab_text_color">@android:color/system_on_error_light</color>
    <color name="emergency_accent">@android:color/system_on_error_light</color>
    <!-- Emergency contacts' heading on the page -->
    <color name="emergency_contacts_text_color">@android:color/system_error_light</color>
    <!-- Tab indicator and action bar accent of the editing screens -->
    <color name="accent_color_dark">@android:color/system_primary_light</color>
</resources>
